**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.git
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.log
deploy/qa-data
deploy/data
data/
qa/

# Never bake configuration into an image. Dockerfile.api, .scheduler and .web
# all do `COPY . .`, so without this the live deploy/.env lands inside the
# backend and scheduler images together with every secret in it. That already
# happened: both shipped /app/deploy/.env plus a timestamped .env backup left
# over from renaming MINIO_* to S3_*. Nothing reads .env at build time --
# Compose supplies it at runtime through env_file -- so excluding it is safe.
#
# No `!env.example` exception here, and it must stay that way: a negation makes
# BuildKit walk the whole context to find what the exception might match, and it
# then fails on root-owned data/postgres despite the data/ rule above. The
# template ships anyway because its name does not start with ".env".
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
